"""L6205D - DMOS dual full-bridge driver, SO20 (STMicroelectronics L6205D013TR).

Datasheet: ST L6205 "DMOS dual full bridge driver", September 2003, 21 pages
(LCSC C962257 copy). Page numbers below refer to that document.

Package: SO20 (16+2+2), ordering code L6205D (p.1). Pin numbers follow the
SO20/PowerDIP20 column of the pin description (p.4). The PowerSO20 part
(L6205PD) numbers the same functions differently (IN1A on pin 6, GND on 1, 10,
11, 20), so it is not a drop-in substitute for this symbol and footprint.

Absolute maximum ratings (p.2):
- VS (VSA = VSB): 60 V. VOD between the bridge A and bridge B power pins: 60 V.
- VBOOT: VS + 10 V.
- VIN, VEN (IN1x, IN2x, ENx): -0.3 to +7 V.
- VSENSEA, VSENSEB: -1 to +4 V.
- IS(peak) per VS pin, tPULSE < 1 ms: 7.1 A (limited by the overcurrent
  protection). IS RMS per VS pin: 2.8 A.
- Tstg, TOP: -40 to 150 C.

Recommended operating conditions (p.2):
- VS: 8 to 52 V (also p.1 "operating supply voltage from 8 to 52 V" and
  Figure 11 "VS 8-52VDC"). VSENSE DC: -1 to +1 V (pulsed, tW < trr: -6 to +6 V).
- IOUT RMS: 2.8 A. Tj: -25 to +125 C. fsw: up to 100 kHz.

Electrical characteristics (p.5-6, Tamb 25 C, VS 48 V):
- UVLO: VSth(ON) 6.6 / 7 / 7.4 V, VSth(OFF) 5.6 / 6 / 6.4 V.
- RDS(ON) at 25 C: high side 0.34 typ / 0.4 max ohm, low side 0.28 / 0.34 ohm.
- Logic inputs: VIL max 0.8 V, VIH min 2 V; Vth(ON) 1.8-2.0 V, Vth(OFF)
  0.8-1.3 V; IIL/IIH +-10 uA. 3.3 V CMOS logic drives them.
- Overcurrent threshold ISOVER (sum per bridge, high side): 4 / 5.6 / 7.1 A.
  Open-drain ON resistance on ENx: 40-60 ohm at 4 mA.
- Dead time 0.5-1 us. Charge-pump frequency 0.6-1 MHz. Thermal shutdown
  165 C typ (p.5, p.11).
- Thermal (p.3): SO20 Rth(j-a) 51 C/W with 6 cm2 of bottom copper, 77 C/W
  with no heat-sinking copper; Rth(j-pins) 14 C/W. The GND pins 5, 6, 15, 16
  are the heat path to the PCB (p.4).

Truth table (p.8): EN low -> both outputs high-Z; EN high: IN1/IN2 = L/L ->
GND/GND, H/L -> VS/GND, L/H -> GND/VS, H/H -> VS/VS.

Required external parts (integrator-owned, p.8 Table 1, Figure 3; p.12 Table 2,
Figure 11):
- Charge pump: D1 (1N4148) from VS to the pump node, D2 (1N4148) from the pump
  node to VBOOT, CBOOT 220 nF from VBOOT to VS, RP 100 ohm + CP 10 nF in series
  from the pump node to VCP. VCP is a 10 V, 600 kHz square wave (p.8).
- ENA, ENB: driven through REN 2.2 k to 180 k (100 k recommended) with CEN to
  GND (5.6 nF recommended), push-pull drive as in Figure 6 or open-drain with
  pull-up as in Figure 5 (p.4 note 6, p.8). The OCD and thermal protection pull
  ENx low through an open-drain MOSFET, so an ENx pin must never be driven
  directly from a push-pull output. An unused EN goes to +5 V through a
  resistor (p.4).
- VS decoupling: a 100-200 nF ceramic between VSA/VSB and GND near the IC,
  plus bulk (Table 2: C1 100 uF, C2 100 nF) (p.12).
- SENSEA, SENSEB: to power ground directly or through a sensing resistor
  (p.4), with the shortest possible trace (p.12). There is no internal
  current regulator on SENSE; the only current protection is the high-side
  OCD (p.9).
- VSA and VSB must be tied to the same supply (p.4): this package exposes one
  VS io for both.
"""

VS = io(Power(voltage="8V to 52V"))
GND = io(Ground)
VBOOT = io(Net)
VCP = io(Net)
IN1A = io(Net)
IN2A = io(Net)
ENA = io(Net)
IN1B = io(Net)
IN2B = io(Net)
ENB = io(Net)
OUT1A = io(Net)
OUT2A = io(Net)
SENSEA = io(Net)
OUT1B = io(Net)
OUT2B = io(Net)
SENSEB = io(Net)

Component(
    name="L6205D",
    symbol=Symbol(library="L6205D.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SOIC127P1032X265-20N.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="L6205D013TR", manufacturer="STMicroelectronics"),
    prefix="IC",
    pins={
        "IN1A": IN1A,
        "IN2A": IN2A,
        "SENSEA": SENSEA,
        "OUT1A": OUT1A,
        "GND": GND,
        "OUT1B": OUT1B,
        "SENSEB": SENSEB,
        "IN1B": IN1B,
        "IN2B": IN2B,
        "ENB": ENB,
        "VBOOT": VBOOT,
        "OUT2B": OUT2B,
        "VSB": VS,
        "VSA": VS,
        "OUT2A": OUT2A,
        "VCP": VCP,
        "ENA": ENA,
    },
)
